WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.800
Dedicated browser profiles separate research history, bookmarks, cookies, settings,

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.856
and accounts from personal browsing.

00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:09.967
Profiles can also separate cases when policy requires stronger boundaries,

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:14.078
but too many profiles become difficult to patch and manage.

00:00:14.078 --> 00:00:19.011
Build a small bookmark structure around workflow: approved search services, official records,

00:00:19.011 --> 00:00:22.711
technical references, archive services, internal policy, and reporting resources.

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:27.233
Review bookmarks periodically because services change, disappear, or alter their terms.

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:29.289
Extensions should be installed carefully.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:34.222
Every extension adds permissions, update dependencies, and potential access to browsing data.

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:38.744
Prefer a minimal approved set, verify the publisher and required permissions,

00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:42.856
and remove tools that no longer provide clear workflow value.

00:00:42.856 --> 00:00:47.789
Screenshot and archive tools should preserve source context, not create isolated fragments.

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:51.489
Record the URL, title, timestamp, and reason for capture.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:55.189
A screenshot is a representation of what was visible,

00:00:55.189 --> 00:00:59.300
while an archive may have coverage gaps or preservation limits.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.644
Keep personal email, social, cloud, and shopping accounts out of the research profile.

00:01:04.644 --> 00:01:07.522
Account separation reduces accidental posting, unwanted personalization,

00:01:07.522 --> 00:01:10.400
and leakage between personal and case activity.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.922
It does not authorize false identities or access to private areas.

00:01:14.922 --> 00:01:18.211
Standardize the environment with documented settings, update checks,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.911
and a known export path into the case structure.

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:27.667
The browser should make collection more consistent while preserving human judgment about source reliability,

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.900
privacy, and scope.
